        <div class="jcBand">
            <div id="pnlJobDescription">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><strong><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;">Why Join DHCS?</span></strong></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;"><span>The Department of Health Care Services (DHCS) is the backbone of California’s health care safety net. Our success is made possible by the hard work of more than 4,800 DHCS team members and through collaboration with the federal government and other state agencies, counties, and partners for the care of low-income families, children, pregnant women, older adults, and persons with disabilities. This is an exciting opportunity to join our diverse team in the following role. If you are interested in joining our team, apply today!</span></span></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;"><span>As the Health Care Financing Manager, you will lead a team focused on improving the lives of Californians. Your main responsibilities will include developing and managing Medi-Cal reimbursement rates and financing policies for Outpatient and Long-Term Care services, ensuring compliance, and advocating for policy changes. You will also oversee provider fees and supplemental reimbursement programs.</span></span></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;"><span>This advertisement includes two or more vacancies within the following teams. Candidates need only apply to this one Job Control to be considered for all vacancies within the teams described below.</span></span></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;"><span>The Long Term Care Section (LTC) oversees critical tasks for long-term care facilities, including setting reimbursement and daily payment rates through annual studies that comply with laws. The Branch focuses on long-term care policies, rate development, and implementation. It conducts rate-setting studies and prepares necessary amendments, bill analyses, and regulations. Teams within the section specialize in programs such as: Financial policies for the Workforce Standards Program, Freestanding Skilled Nursing Facility rates, and various subacute services. Financial models for Distinct Part Nursing Facilities and Rural Swing Beds. Programs may be reassigned based on need.</span></span></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;"><span>The Provider Rates Branch (PRB) establishes outpatient provider rates and financing policies for Medi-Cal Fee-For-Service. It updates payment policies, sets reimbursement rates, and manages provider fees and supplemental payments. The PRB develops State Plan Amendments, conducts studies, analyzes regulations, and collaborates with stakeholders on rate topics.</span></span></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;"><span>PRB consists of four teams including MCO Tax Provider Rate Increases and other health care services. It also has two units that conduct analytical studies and review policies related to the Medi-Cal managed care system, CYBHI, CalAIM Waivers, TRI, and hospital financial policy. Programs within the division are interchangeable based on need.</span></span></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;"><span>The Capitated Rates Development Division (CRDD) focuses on financial modeling and capitation rate policy for various health care services, including MCO Tax Provider Rate Increases and Hospital Directed Payments. It includes two units that conduct analytical studies, surveys, and make recommendations on administrative matters relevant to the Medi-Cal managed care system, CYBHI, CalAIM Waivers, and Medi-Cal hospital financial policy. Programs within the division are typically interchangeable based on need.</span></span></span></p><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=25873734&name=SSMIDUTYSTATEMENT(12.12.24).pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
                </p>
            
</div>

            <div id="pnlWorkingConditions">
	
